{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1392836-epic-spells-in-m20","id":1392836,"title":"Epic spells in M20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-30T10:24:13-07:00","id":1392836,"title":"Epic spells in M20?","content":"So AFAIK M20 omits archspheres, which means all effects of them are folded into the single level 5 spheres. But how will you deal with some spells which should be considered &quot;epic&quot; or being related with archspheres? (Mind you, I mean ONLY 5 LEVELS EXIST, IGNORE HORIZON: THE STRONGHOLD OF HOPE PLEASE)<br /> <br /> For example,<br /> 1. the most famous one which can turn a vampire into the mortal, needs Prime 6 and several level 4 spheres, or any other spell which can edit the supernatural curse<br /> 2. Remove the Permandox, which needs Prime 9 in MotA<br /> 3. Edit the mechanics, making you buy Abilities cheaper, for example(Thousand Whispers in KotE can do this, though)<br /> 4. Gift you with Metis &amp; Flaws, like making you have True Faith (A KotE Rites can do this, in a very hard way, though)<br /> ...<br /> <br /> Would you treat them as &quot;merely&quot; master spells?<br /> One of the thoughts I have is to set a limitation on Arete, treating it like Generation or Dharma. Some epic spells can only be accessible to high Arete (6+). But this may be a bad idea though, Mage doesn't work like Vampire or Kindred of the East, it shouldn't have such bounds<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T10:51:04-07:00","id":1392844,"title":"","content":"I've always found these &quot;Epic Effects&quot; to be more story/plot based than anything to be taken seriously. In such a case multiple master level spheres, followed by &quot;Great Work&quot; rituals and 50+ successes I'd say most anything can be accomplished for the good of the story.<br /> <br /> Beyond that many arch-sphere effects have so many provisions and drawbacks that they become stories in themselves to achieve. Allowing a master level mage to perform them in that fashion should be fine. Allowing them &quot;willy-nilly&quot; seems like a recipe for disaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:37:30-07:00","id":1392860,"title":"","content":"I think Arete is a reasonable way to limit the grander effects. After all, no mage can have sphere levels higher than their Arete anyway, so the idea of it as a ceiling is already built into the game. It would make sense to me that turning a vampire mortal requires a higher level of enlightenment/comprehension of the nature of magic and the universe than some of the more standard (though still impressive) level five sphere abilities. <br /> <br /> But another way to limit could be to set a very high number of successes, which can only be made manageable by obtaining certain story-appropriate things to proceed. For example: let's say my players are a group of Celestial Choristers out to cure a vampire. First, of course, they'd have to find or create an appropriate ritual. Then, I'd expect them to find and secure a suitable location with appropriate resonance (perhaps the Basilica of Saint Peter?), practice appropriate artifacts that would be part of the rite (Maybe some vessel belonging to a saint), they should have a good source of quintessence, and probably a good number of other mages to assist. That kind of thing.<br /> <br /> The characters' attempts to obtain each element would probably be a story in its own right, and each element would reduce the required number of successes to a point where eventually the ritual might actually be feasible. Eventually.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:53:28-07:00","id":1392866,"title":"","content":"Arete is equal to Generation or Dharma in some ways, although some people oppose this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T12:13:42-07:00","id":1392876,"title":"","content":"There are several ways to go about this. Here are a few:<br /> <br /> Use the archspheres of previous editions. I didn't like them though, so I made my own.<br /> <br /> Make your own archspheres. Which is a lot of trouble, but you could also use mine. I'll fish them up if anyone asks. <br /> <br /> Use Sphere 6 as sphere 6+<br /> <br /> Or maybe have your mage players think outside the box. For example:<br /> <br /> Turning a vampire mortal should start with life 5 and matter 5 to turn an animate corpse into a mortal human. Most likely, though, you'd need to create something like a functioning soul (prime 5 and spirit 5 maybe?) Or drag that human's soul from wherever it is (maybe using correspondence 4, and spirit 4 and a reverse exorcism). But then there's the ancient curse thing which will probably require the forgiveness of the being that cursed Cain (as a sort of quest), the intercession of a powerful divinity (maybe with some quests performed for an appropriate deity followed by the appropriate curse lifting ritual), enough true faith, or something drastic like transforming the vampire into a new person (mind 5 and a different body and mind... Or rather, you just used the vampire as raw material) who will now be so metaphysically different from the vampire that the curse can't possibly apply. Or how about using Time with successes enough to reach the curse's creation, and entropy 5 to destroy the ancient link of the curse to the human. <br /> <br /> (So maybe Life 5, matter 5, time 5, entropy 5, and either spirit 5 and prime 5 or spirit 4 and correspondence 4) each step requiring successes and for a truly lasting effect maybe requiring quint per roll like a wonder.<br /> <br /> Removing permadox always seemed like something for prime 5 plus the use of the spheres related to what the permanent paradox is lodged in (a material thing? A living body? A soul? A mind?) and expending quintessence. <br /> <br /> I guess I'd let people sustain permanent ability increases using mind 4 or 5, and maybe life , 2 or 3for very physical abilities.<br /> <br /> I would say each merit and flaw would require its own spell. True faith would probably require a comprehensive editing of both mind and spirit, possibly needing some prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T12:54:30-07:00","id":1392882,"title":"","content":"For a truly Epic Effect? Pattern it after the creation of a Talisman: <i>at a minimum</i>, require the expenditure of Personal Quintessence into each Arete roll, and cap it off with a dot of Willpower which then has to be bought back with Experience. <br /> <br /> Second, don't neglect the Instruments. There's a reason my house rule for discarding Instruments keys it to ranks rather than Spheres (as in earlier editions) or individual Instruments (as in M20): in my opinion, you shouldn't be able to discard your Instruments for a Master-level Effect until you have achieved the highest Arete possible. <br /> <br /> Furthermore, while there aren't any hard and fast rules on this, not all Instruments are created equal; some are more inconvenient to use than others. And the more successes an Effect requires \u2014 that is, the bigger the working is \u2014 the more inconvenient the Instruments need to be. For truly Epic Effects, your usual Instruments don't cut it; identifying, acquiring, and setting up the appropriate Instruments should be stories in and of themselves. Use the rules for acquiring Quintessence as a guideline for how much effort needs to go into an Epic Effect's Instruments; the main difference between collecting Quintessence and preparing an Epic Effect's Instruments is that the former explicitly requires dots in Prime; the latter does not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T12:56:28-07:00","id":1392883,"title":"","content":"I've always been of the opinion that epic spells should be a matter of preparation and skill. Not having sphere ranks above 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T13:05:09-07:00","id":1392885,"title":"","content":"Exactly, though I would also add \u201cdedication\u201d. The first part of my last post was focused on that, whole the rest of it was dedicated to preparation. Skill is well enough covered as is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}